{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310583,"nonce":"UQidGo0C75AAzLPkCJM0RD6HpVU=","title":"FULLY FIXED in commits 48d24ef + b60f975. Cross-file warnings now correctly attribute to source file AND line AND column AND highlighted ...","message":"**Status: OPEN.** Partially-mitigated in commit `c012003` (debug-dump shows real origin file; SourceMap render path covers imports).\n\n\n`rayzor run Main.hx` (no args) prints ~20 E0382 warnings AND ~10 W0014 advisories AND THEN the usage banner. Every warning header reads `Main.hx:\u003cline\u003e:\u003ccol\u003e` even though the variables (`text`, `prompt`, `ids`, `nextId`, `weights`, `info`, `result`, `tok`, `out`) live in cross-file modules (`nue/tokenizer/BPETokenizer.hx`, `nue/sampling/GenerationLoop.hx`, `nue/arch/BertArch.hx`, etc).\n\nThe cited \"value moved here\" / \"value used here after move\" spans land on comments or unrelated code lines in Main.hx (e.g. `pushRecent(id);` cited for a `text` warning; doc-comments cited for `info` warnings).\n\n\nPost-commit `c012003` (which populates `typed_file.metadata.file_path`):\n\n```\n[E0382-DEBUG] var=text typed_file=.../nue/tokenizer/BPETokenizer.hx\n              use_file_id=0 use_line=116 use_col=17\n\n[E0382-DEBUG] var=prompt typed_file=.../nue/sampling/GenerationLoop.hx\n              use_file_id=0 use_line=99 use_col=16\n\n[E0382-DEBUG] var=weights typed_file=.../nue/arch/BertArch.hx\n              use_file_id=0 use_line=119 use_col=27\n```\n\nSo `typed_file.metadata.file_path` IS correct (BPETokenizer / GenerationLoop / BertArch), but `use_file_id` AND `move_file_id` are **always 0** for every cross-file violation. The renderer correctly resolves file_id=0 → Main.hx and uses the line/byte_offset as offsets INTO Main.hx — hence the bizarre attribution.\n\n\nThe bug is in **upstream span propagation**, not in the renderer or the ownership-check site. Spans inside imported TypedFiles carry file_id=0 instead of the file's real file_id. The `span_converter` is correctly initialised per-file (per `lowering.initialize_span_converter_with_filename` at `compilation.rs:4747`), but the bookkeeping doesn't reach the spans on TypedExpressions / TypedStatements that ownership analysis consumes.\n\n\n1. **`typed_file.metadata.file_path` setter in `lower_file`** (~16 LOC). Was always empty; now correctly populated from `file.filename`. Makes RAYZOR_DEBUG_E0382 useful for triaging. Required prerequisite for any deeper fix that uses the typed_file's identity.\n\n2. **`build_full_source_map` helper unifying the two renderer paths** (~30 LOC). `print_mir_diagnostics` previously added only `user_files` to its SourceMap; `print_compilation_errors` had the full set (user + stdlib + import_hx + on-demand-compiled). They drifted. Both now use the helper. No behaviour change for already-correct file_ids; ensures any future fix that sets file_id correctly will render to the right source.\n\n\nTried in `c012003` (then reverted before commit): override `use_location.file_id` at diagnostic-creation time by looking up `typed_file.metadata.file_path` against `user_files / stdlib_files / import_hx_files / compiled_files`. The path lookup returned None even with `std::fs::canonicalize` normalisation because the import file's path was registered somewhere not in those four lists. The override was a band-aid anyway; real fix is upstream.\n\n\n1. Instrument `populate_ownership_stmts` to print the file_id captured on each TypedStatement before recording into the ownership graph. Confirm whether file_id is already 0 at TypedStatement creation, or becomes 0 somewhere between TAST construction and ownership analysis.\n\n2. Check `lower_file` / span_converter coupling: does `lowering.initialize_span_converter_with_filename(file_id, ...)` actually set a file_id that flows into TypedExpression spans? Or is there a separate counter?\n\n3. Grep for `SourceLocation::new\\|file_id: 0\\|file_id::FileId(0)` in the lowering pass — many initialisers may hardcode 0.\n\n4. The likely fix: thread the lower_file's `file_id` argument all the way down through `lower_class` → `lower_method` → `lower_expression` → TypedExpression construction so each TypedExpression's span carries the file's real file_id.\n\n\n- [[project-move-clone-enforced]] — added the RAYZOR_DEBUG_E0382 dump (workflow `wlxn3joln`) precisely because of this attribution bug; the dump was needed to triangulate real source files\n- The `nueFix` agent's note in that workflow: \"The diagnostic printer mislabels every cross-file ownership violation as Main.hx — the line numbers point into the correct file but the basename is wrong, which made the audit harder than it should be (potential follow-up: thread the typed_file path through `check_ownership_violations` so `var_name` and the file label come from the same TypedFile).\"\n- That assessment is partially confirmed and partially refined: the typed_file IS the right one (post-c012003), but the file_id on the violation's location is still wrong.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_diagnostic_span_file_id_always_zero` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}